course: dictionary
lesson: 84
title: What is an actor?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An actor is a person who plays a part in a play, a show or a film. When you watch a film, the people pretending to be the characters are the actors.
explain: «Actors in a play rely on each other's lines; if one forgets, the others are left stuck on stage.» Here the actors are the people on stage saying the lines. Check the meaning: does "a person who plays a part" fit the sentence? It does.
explain: The word can also mean any person or group that takes part in something. «In an audition people try out, and the director chooses who fits each part.» The context tells you which meaning is used.
fact: An actor plays a part in a play, a show or a film.
fact: «Actors» is the plural; «actress» is used for a woman, though «actor» is used for all.
fact: A «stunt double» is a trained stunt performer who stands in for an actor in the dangerous moments.
fact: The Greeks invented theatre, and their actors performed in open-air theatres, wearing masks.
fact: In drama class, actors learn lines and roles.
exercise: «Actors in a play rely on each other's lines.» Who are the actors in this sentence? | People who clean the theatre | People who sit in the audience and clap | *People who play parts in a play | People who sell tickets at the door
exercise: «A stunt double stands in for an actor in the dangerous moments.» What is a stunt double? | A person who writes the lines | The director of the film | *A trained stunt performer who stands in for an actor | A famous actor who never gets hurt
exercise: Ruby says «actor» only means a man. What is the best answer? | Yes, actors are always men | *Actress is used for a woman, but actor is used for all | Actors are the people who build the stage | Actors are only in films, not plays
test: «Many famous actors started with tiny roles.» What does this tell you about small parts? | *They matter, and many famous actors began with them | Small parts are always in films | Only famous people get small parts | They are not worth doing
test: Which phrase from the lessons means the main actor in a show? | *Lead actor | Ticket seller | Audience member | Stage hand
exam: «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed by actors wearing masks.» What were the actors wearing in Greek theatre? | Helmets | Crowns | *Masks | Capes
